        "descriptionHtml": "<p>The group does not intercept member <code>click</code>s: <code>GroupController</code> only listens to <code>change</code> on the host in the capture phase, and button-group uses a purely presentational context that does not even implement <code>handleChange</code>, so member clicks bubble through the group host unchanged.</p>\n<p><code>event.target</code> is that member host—one handler catches the whole group and uses <code>data-id</code> to tell which member it was (button delegates only <code>aria-label</code> to the inner button and leaves other attributes on the host without copying them into the shadow, so <code>data-*</code> is safe as an identity marker).</p>\n<p>Members with <code>disabled</code> and <code>loading</code> still produce no click, so the readout does not move.</p>\n<p>Grouping does not change form behavior either: a member with <code>type=\"submit\"</code> still submits the outer <code>&lt;form></code>, so clicking \"Save\" first reads <code>Clicked save</code> and is then overwritten by the submit event.</p>\n<p>button-group has no <code>disabled</code> of its own: to disable the whole group, put it inside <code>&lt;fieldset disabled></code> (members are disabled through form-level disabling and turn gray together), or write it on each member.</p>",
