        "descriptionHtml": "<p><code>disabled</code> only suppresses the menu: a right-click does not open it, and the trigger area itself is neither greyed out nor recolored—the component renders no menu surface at all, so there is nothing to grey out, and disabling a context menu is not the same as disabling the trigger area.</p>\n<p>The button below toggles <code>disabled</code>, and the area text follows the state; the readout records <code>open-change</code>, so right-clicks do not count while disabled, and opening works as usual once it is re-enabled.</p>",
