        "descriptionHtml": "<p><code>controlled</code> hands the closing decision to the page: Escape, backdrop click, and the closable button do not change <code>open</code>; they only dispatch <code>open-change</code> to request closing.</p>\n<p>If the page does not write back, the dialog stays open, and the <code>&lt;output></code> accumulates the number of blocked requests; \"Discard changes\" in the footer writes <code>false</code> directly, which is a programmatic close that <code>controlled</code> does not intercept.</p>",
