        "id": "container-width",
        "title": "Container width",
        "descriptionHtml": "<p>The width comes from the container and is recomputed when the container changes: narrower cuts harder, wider takes truncation back. The two boxes below have percentage widths, each with a cap—the cap guarantees overflow even on a wide screen, otherwise the whole string fits once the window is wide enough and nothing is visible in the box. Drag the window width to watch both lines re-cut.</p>",
